From 2ca4febaabc5793d1863b423c24ff460d42a15c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:26:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Touch controls: two-thumb options, scroll strip, launcher
 settings wired up

Lets one thumb attack/shove and aim while the other moves, without a
third finger. Everything is off by default and set in the touch editor.

Per key/mouse button (tap a button in the editor):
- Drag to aim: while a finger is held on the button, dragging it also
  moves the cursor like PAD mode (8 pt dead zone; speed slider in the
  editor panel appears once any button uses it).
- Long press to lock: pressing for a set time (default 0.5 s, adjustable
  per button, 0.2-2 s) keeps the button held after the finger lifts
  (gold ring + haptic), e.g. RC for hands-free aiming. The next tap, ESC,
  hiding the controls, or connecting a controller lets go. Only in the
  Default fire mode.
- Fire mode: Default (held while pressed), Auto (held and re-pressed
  every 0.25 s) or Release (holding does nothing and shows amber, so you
  can aim without spamming; lifting the finger sends one press).

New controls (Add menu):
- Fire mode toggle: pick the button it changes ("Changes"); each tap in
  game switches that button between Default and Release (DEF/REL).
- Scroll strip: a tall bar; sliding a finger on it sends mouse-wheel
  notches at the cursor, so containers scroll (and the world zooms)
  with one thumb. Scroll speed and reverse direction in the panel.

Also:
- The overlay now honours settings the launcher already had but the
  public overlay ignored: Settings > Controls > Two-Finger Zoom
  ("zom.twoFingerZoom"; off removes the two-finger scroll gesture), the
  editor's PAD Sensitivity ("zom.mouseSens") and Aim stick attack
  ("zom.aimAttackMode": Release attacks once when the stick is let go,
  Auto holds the attack while it is pushed; cancelled touches never
  attack).
- Opacity can go down to 5% (was 30% in the editor, 20% in game), and
  the editor shows the value.
- The editor settings panel scrolls when it is taller than the screen,
  so Add/Done stay reachable.

